      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3z-1)\\,\\text{d}z=$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting up the difference and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3z-1)\\,\\text{d}z & =3{\\int }_{-1}^{0}z\\,\\text{d}z-{\\int }_{-1}^{0}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}-z\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{z}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}-z\\,{|}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({0}^{2}-(-1)^{2})-(0-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}-1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
