    "q-114199": {
      "dom_id": "step-q114199",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{2y}-y)\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "We split the integral into the difference of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\frac{1}{2y}-y)\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y-{\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|\\,{|}_{1}^{e}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-0)-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
